<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνδον</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>within</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.98
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦσαν ἡμῖν ἔ. ἑπτὰ μναῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					19.22
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				27.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένες ἔ. ἐῖσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.337
				</span></i>
			,al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραδίη ἔ. ὑλάκτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἄνδον οὐχ οὕτω φρονῶν</span>
			<i>in one's heart</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1514
			</span></i> (troch.; but lit. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἄ. ἀνακάλλυνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.Com.
					2D.
				</span></i>
			); <i>at home</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				310e
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔ</span>. those <i>of
				the house</i>, the <i>family</i>, esp. the
			<i>domestics</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				155
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				677
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				213c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἄνδον</span>
			<i>family matters, household affairs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				334
			</span></i>, etc.; also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔ.</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1017
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔ. καθήμενοι</span> the
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.43
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς ἔ., Ζεφύροιο ἔ.</span>,
				<i>in the house</i> of Zeus, of Zephyrus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.200
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ κεύθετ᾽ ἔ. καρδίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					102
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηνῆς ἔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				218
			</span></i> (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				320d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ὢν αὑτοῦ</span>
			<i>master of</i> oneself, self-possessed, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.45
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶν φρενῶν οὐκ ἔ. ὤν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					709
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. γενοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					233
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔ. ἔ. ἐστίν</span> with
			a play on signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				396
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> uses it c. dat. as strengthd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				3.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.44
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				203
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>below</i>, in a book, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. γέγραπται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					5.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> with Verbs of
			motion, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				7.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				9.61
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδοτέρω</span>
			.</div>
